        "categoryId": "identity-recognition",
        "strongestReasonBelowThree": "Pilot-specific identity depends on a Polsten that is only a few pixels at 256 px. The contact sheet frames the vehicle too small to show it at all.",
        "resolved": true,
        "resolutionEvidence": [
          {
            "kind": "technical-record",
            "recordId": "polish-r22/independent-review.json",
            "observation": "In my 256 px downscales, r22's dark ring is a legible dark donut in ortho front, az-0 and az-315, a clear gain over r21. The contact-sheet framing remains a presentation issue, not a model defect.",
            "evidenceSha256": "bb4d3e9e2edcd07401c6cf8880edf54867f1bd090503512b7e414ebf6f6dd245"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "categoryId": "silhouette",
        "strongestReasonBelowThree": "The new boss adds a lumpy, faceted mound with a re-entrant kink to the turret-front profile.",
        "resolved": true,
        "resolutionEvidence": [
          {
            "kind": "technical-record",
            "recordId": "polish-r22/independent-review.json",
            "observation": "This is visible only at close-up. At gameplay scale the change is a sub-40 px cluster, and the major contours are unchanged.",
            "evidenceSha256": "bb4d3e9e2edcd07401c6cf8880edf54867f1bd090503512b7e414ebf6f6dd245"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "categoryId": "mechanical-coherence",
        "strongestReasonBelowThree": "The flange should be fixed to the turret, but it is parented to the articulated Polsten ball (P09 -> M.polsten-ball). If the ball elevates or traverses, the flange would tilt off the boss land and either gap or interpenetrate. No posed evidence exists. A dark inboard wedge pocket also remains where the spot-face cut meets the cheek.",
        "resolved": false
      },
